{"id": "tea:yogabija:topic.ha-tha", "source": "src:yogabija", "location": {"ref": "topic.ha-tha"}, "paraphrase": "'Ha' is said to be the sun and 'ṭha' the moon; the union of sun and moon is called haṭhayoga.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice", "sound-language"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U28-hatha-texts"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A10", "D"], "notes": "Topic-level locator: exact chapter/verse not recalled (to be supplied in Phase D). The Jyotsnā on HYP 1.1 quotes the same verse as from the Siddhasiddhāntapaddhati (see tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika-jyotsna:1.1).", "concepts": ["cpt:meaning-of-hatha", "cpt:sun-moon-fire"], "terms": ["trm:hatha", "trm:surya", "trm:candra"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U28-hatha-texts"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogabija:topic.knowledge-and-yoga", "source": "src:yogabija", "location": {"ref": "topic.knowledge-and-yoga"}, "paraphrase": "Knowledge without yoga does not bring liberation: even one devoted to knowledge, dispassionate, knowing dharma and with senses conquered — even a god — does not gain liberation without yoga; yoga and knowledge together liberate.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["dispute", "karma-liberation"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U28-hatha-texts"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A10", "D"], "notes": "Topic-level locator: exact chapter/verse not recalled (to be supplied in Phase D).", "disputes": ["dsp:yoga-or-knowledge-for-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:ripe-and-unripe-body"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U28-hatha-texts"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogabija:topic.mahayoga", "source": "src:yogabija", "location": {"ref": "topic.mahayoga"}, "paraphrase": "Yoga, though called fourfold — mantra, laya, haṭha and rāja — is one 'great yoga' (mahāyoga).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U28-hatha-texts"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A10", "D"], "notes": "Topic-level locator: exact chapter/verse not recalled (to be supplied in Phase D).", "concepts": ["cpt:four-yogas", "cpt:mahayoga-unity"], "terms": ["trm:mahayoga"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U28-hatha-texts"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogabija:topic.ripe-body", "source": "src:yogabija", "location": {"ref": "topic.ripe-body"}, "paraphrase": "The body is of two kinds, unripe and ripe; the unripe body, not fired by yoga, is subject to karma, disease and death; the ripe body is fired by yoga, and only the one whose body is ripened is liberated.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "causal", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["body-layers", "karma-liberation"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U28-hatha-texts"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A10", "D"], "notes": "Topic-level locator: exact chapter/verse not recalled (to be supplied in Phase D).", "concepts": ["cpt:ripe-and-unripe-body", "cpt:kaya-siddhi"], "terms": ["trm:pakva-deha"], "disputes": ["dsp:yoga-or-knowledge-for-liberation"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U28-hatha-texts"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
